t is happening  my daughter was only nine  john the new orleans police detective  and love of her life  died six years later i've been through a  lot of life's changes and if i can help  somebody else navigate it a little bit  easier  then there's a purpose for all of it  that's a saying in new orleans ain't  dare no more  that purpose has helped to push her to  walk away from a successful career on  television and run a company called  life's about change it's her company her  idea  to sell products that are made by people  who've changed their lives  methamphetamine i started at the age of  15.  went to prison at the age of 20. i  had my first child at 16 and i didn't  know how to navigate that and so  i started using opiates at 18. jenna and  amanda are now successful potters who  imprint karen's line of coffee mugs with  words to live by we have faith kindness  peace we're living testimonies of what a  life can look like changed so the idea  with the candles is what  so the idea from the candles came from a  doctor who was helping my husband and i  to navigate his cancer journey  and the day he was diagnosed she said i  want you to go get a candle and then i  want you to watch the wax disappear and  the wax in your cancer cells you said  visualize it what's your intention for  folks who buy the candle from you i hope  that they see the flame and they think  about their own inner strength life's  about change started as a t-shirt  company this might be my favorite time  for change  single again  good afternoon i'm karen swenson for  several years now karen swenson has  juggled that job at wwl tv  with finding special vendors the candles  that we have those are created by an  american veteran joins the military at  33 because she's decided it's time to  give back  and that seems to me to be the  underlining of the company that's it  it's the focus on the present and the  gratitude and the joy that comes with it  always  look for the positive or at least try  to be in a state of joy it will help you  navigate it so when my husband was sick  we looked for the person who beat it  when he passed i looked for the widow  who was still smiling  karen's website is filled with stories  like that but there is one story not  there the one that hit hard after her  appendicitis  so as i'm  recuperating and i pull up the pathology  reports  and fully expecting to be fine and it  said carcinoma  and i was like  no way  and all of a sudden they said uh  had you not had this other pain your  appendix that kind of cancer is so  insidious  that by the time you usually find it's  over i don't like even speaking about it  because to me it gives it it gives it  strength you some power and that's why i  never talked about it before honestly  but did that period help drive you to  give the final word to your boss that  i'm hanging it up  this twist of fate that has saved my  life right right so yes and you start  thinking maybe it's time to  untether yourself from the desk and just  sort of blindly go out there and just  trust the universe so it is not goodbye  i am not leaving new orleans i'm just  pivoting life is about change and it's  time i live up to the mantra so here we  go a new adventure after one heck of a  ride so  thank you new orleans here's to you  cheers  [Applause]  david once again i'm telling you you  find the most amazing people i'm  thinking about karen swenson massive  tumor  her home's destroyed her husband dies of  cancer she has appendicitis and yet she  still has figured out a way to find the  positive i'm in awe of this woman  she's the brightest light on television  gail i never met the woman before this  but when i heard she was retiring and  walking away why would karen swenson  leave television you were the queen in  new orleans and she's doing it because  there's got to be a bigger purpose a  better purpose a more fulfilling purpose  that also gives back everything by the  way that's involved in our company is  ameri